# Local env with real values (the API URL is not secret, but keep the file out of git).
# The glob, not just `.env.local`: the documented local file is `.env.development.local`, so a
# bare `.env.local` entry would leave the one people actually create committable.
.env*.local

# OpenNext build output.
.open-next/

# Generated by Next on every dev/build, and it churns: the import inside it points at
# `.next/dev/types/…` after `next dev` and `.next/types/…` after `next build`. Committing it
# also made `tsc` fail on a fresh clone, because that import target does not exist until
# something has been built. Verified that typecheck passes without the file at all.
next-env.d.ts
